NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1069,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,4,2,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.5192,"rank":0.0805,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ022008","role":"top","render":{"description":"An old spinster often had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. Once she refused to give way to","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20911","half":"top"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ045418","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It is a forewarning. Ticking can often be heard too. That is also a forewarning: a house will later be renovated.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ111402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But when they go to look, the neighbour is simply asleep. The mother suspects that something is going to happen. It was indeed an omen: ten weeks later the neighbour's child drowns and the same wailing is heard.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ123209","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Nurses are often keen to get cauls because carrying one keeps them safe. (After all, if you carry a caul, you are bulletproof.) Cauls are also often sold on. Many Freemasons are said to have a caul.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0489"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0432","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The next day the neighbour's house on the side that was hot is on fire.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0491"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ022008","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"something she saw coming, and she got a crack in her head. When she grew too old to get out of bed at night, she opened the curtains and saw everything through the window.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ019214","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"These are omens: shortly afterwards her little sister is killed in a traffic accident. The funeral takes place exactly as the girl saw it earlier.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ065302","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He stepped over it. Two weeks later an old fellow from the neighbourhood died, and the hearse really came by.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CJ007616","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man pulls him aside when a funeral procession passes. The narrator does not see the procession.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CJ109402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The door and the gate are opened, and he is driven to a house where someone has died. On the way back the gate is opened for him again, but he has seen no one.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"CJ111119","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"They were the portents of the later bicycle, car and train lights. Other people saw the train running before the railway was there. It was a vision of the future.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"CJ014011","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The next day the train from Leeuwarden to Groningen ran for the first time.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0492"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"DYKFRIES2201","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Likewise, here and there people heard the roar of trains, years before there was any talk of railways in Friesland.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0492"},"home":"1-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0481. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c6"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c6"],"stack":["c1","c6"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1418,"rank":0.2835,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ070902","role":"member","render":{"description":"People once saw a farm on fire. But when they came closer, nothing was wrong. Later the farm really burned down.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27979","original":"Myn wiif fortelde wolris dat to Sybrandahûs - tusken Dokkum en Rinsumageast - seagen lju yn 'e nacht in boereplaets yn 'e brân. Hja hearden allerhande lûden en stemmen fan minsken. Sy gongen der hinne, mar der wie neat.\nLetter is dy plaets troch de tonger opbrând.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ088406","role":"member","render":{"description":"A man once saw a farmhouse on fire, but when he came closer, nothing turned out to be wrong. Later the farm did burn down after all.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33288","original":"yn 'e brân. 't Wie by de earste bocht as men gyng fan 'e brêge fan 'e Harkema nei Surhústerfean. Mar doe't omke der by kom, brânde 't net.\nLetter is dat spul ôfbrând.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEMP295","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A boy is released from being a werewolf when his pelt gets burnt. His friends helped him with this unintentionally.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43420","original":"De weerwolf verlost\n\nTe Blitterswijk woonde een jonge man die de naam had des nachts uit weerwolven te gaan. Enige vrienden wilden echter wel eens bij die gedaanteverwiseling tegenwoordig zijn. Zij gingen daarom een avond naar zijn huis en zetten zich om de haard. Het ging op middernacht aan en daar niemand sprak van naar huis gaan, zweette de weerwolf water en bloed van benauwdheid. Hij wilde de deur uit, maar zijn kameraden beletten hem dit en hielden hem stevig vast.\nToen het middernacht sloeg, viel opeens een groot wolfsvel uit de schoorsteen in het vuur. De weerwolf begon te schreeuwen als een bezetene en stelde zich aan als een duivel. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ037801","role":"member","render":{"description":"A boy and a girl once saw a fire from a distance, but when they came closer there was no fire at all. A year later a fire did break out at that spot.","place":"Kollum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0491","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23086","original":"It is jierren lyn. Ik en myn feint kommen us fan Sweagerfean. Wy moesten nei de Triemen ta. Wy roannen de Úlke-loane del by Swagerfean. Doe't wy sahwat midden op 'e loane wienen, en oer de feart seagen, seinen wy: \"Sjoch, dêr is brân!\"\nDêr woenen wy hinne en sa kommen wy op 'e Trekwei. Mar dêr wie neat to sjen. Alles wie tsjuster.\nIn jier nei dy tiid briek dêr brân út op in pleats, krekt op datselde plak, dêr't wy de brân sjoen hienen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Broek belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1323,"rank":0.3975,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"Voda_022_16","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A clergyman saw his own funeral. Four men with a bier kept walking behind him all night. He later died on that same road.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/129749","original":"Een geestelijke uit Oirschot zag eens zijn eigen begrafenis. Op een nacht ging hij van Oirschot naar Best. Daar hoorde hij achter zich iemand lopen. Toen ie omkeek, zag ie vier mannen die een baar droegen. Hij wilde wachten, maar toen hie stil bleef staan, bleven ook de dragers stilstaan. En als ie verder ging, gingen ook de dragers verder. Zo bleven deze vier mannen met de baar de gehele nacht achter de geestelijke lopen. Die was blij dat ie eindelijk in Best aankwam, waar hij van de schrik kon bekomen. Enige tijd later moest de geestelijke weer naar Best. Daar stierf hij plotseling. Toen droeg men het lijk van de geestelijke over dezelfde weg die hij gelopen had toen de dragers met de baar hem volgden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ104404","role":"omen","render":{"description":"The evening before IJe shot four policemen dead, the sky already turned red, as a foreshadowing of the blood.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37442","original":"De jouns fan tofoaren foardat de fjouwer plysjes troch IJe Wykstra fan Greategast deasketten waerden wie de loft alhiel read. Dit hat in foarboade west fan it bloedbad.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ057808","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A young couple once saw a great light on the way back. When she got home the girl asked her father why the light was on. The father said the light was not on, and that if she had seen a great light anyway, it was an omen. Four weeks later the man was dead.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25929","original":"Frou van der Molen - hjir út 'e Pein - en har earste man wienen us op in joun fuort west to praten. 't Wie hjir achter yn 'e Juliana-buert. Sy wienen noch net troud. Doe stienen se ynienen yn 't ljocht. Sy wienen noch net oan hûs ta.\nDoe't se thús kommen sei se tsjin har heit: \"Hwerom ha jim de lampe sa heech brânnen?\"\nDoe sei har heit: \"Wy ha de lampe net op hawn. Mar astû hjir in ljocht sjoen hast, dan gebeurt der aenst hwat.\"\nFjouwer wiken letter wie har heit dea.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","4 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":4},"on_success":{"chime":4,"digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.5498,"rank":0.6634,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ115106","role":"target","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot witte wieven (white women) always haunt around midnight.","place":null,"prov":"Fr.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/31040","original":"By 't Tiltsje tusken Eastemar en Sumar spûken om 12 ûre yn 'e nacht altyd wite wiven.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KEUNING012603","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Two white women are said to walk in the churchyard at night.","place":"Genum","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131651","original":"Der waerd ek sein, dat op it tsjerkhôf to Hegebeintum by nacht faek twa wite wiven omrounen.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-1","geo":[53.32481,5.87511]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ019805","role":"helper","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot, wandering witte wieven (white women) hang with their arms over the gates.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20537","original":"To Feankleaster, by de beide slotten, dêr spoeket it. Guon ha dêr wite wiven spoekjen sjoen. By de daem hingje soms sokke wiven mei de earms oer de hekke hinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-1","geo":[53.25731,6.0363]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"YPFOE070d","role":"helper","render":{"description":"The narrator is heading home with a few friends. On the way they meet a white girl moving quickly. She floats towards a cottage. They go to investigate. Later an old man hanged himself, and people say it was connected with this. The minister is very sceptical about the story.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12149","original":"Wite juffers\nWat ik hjir yn 'e Westerein sels sjoen ha. Dat is no lyn, ik tink sa'n fiif-, seis-, sânenfyftich jier. Myn kammeraat en ik gyngen de jûntiid om in oere of alve stadichoan nei hûs ta. Doe troffen wy in pear jongelju en dy hâlden ús oan. De man sei: 'Sjoch, wat is dêr? Dêr is in famke midden yn 'e sûkerei. By it hûs dêre is it allegearre út en tsjuster, mar hoe kin dan sa'n wyt famke der yn 't lân weze?' Doe seach ik it ek. Ik sei: 'Dan moatte wy dêr ris even sjen'. Mar dat famke avensrarde tige hurd en wy koenen sjen, dat it net gie, mar dat it sweefde. It hie de grutte sawat fan in gewoan famke, en sniewyt. Ik sei: 'No, sille wy ris sjen? …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-1","geo":[53.17734,5.8037]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of De Westereen.","Find Hurdegaryp on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.21333,5.94137],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Hurdegaryp"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.4374,"rank":1.1941,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ103913","role":"member","render":{"description":"One evening a man thought he recognised his niece in a woman coming towards him. However, he was lifted up and thrown away, after which the woman floated off.","place":"Drogeham","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37327","original":"It gebeurde op 'e Ikkers op in joun dat Harm Hamstra bûtendoar kaem en in frommeske seach. Hy miende dat it syn nichtsje wie, in jongfaem fan sa'n tweintich jier: Wytske Hamstra, dy't letter troude mei Elle Wijma fan Eastemar. Hja kaem him yn 'e mjitte.\nHy sei: \"Bistû dêr noch, Wytske?\"\nMar dyselde sei neat werom. Ynpleats dêrfan wied er opnom woarn en in ein fuortsmiten en dat frommeske wie swevend fuortrekke.\nOp 'e weromreis kom er wer by ús tolânne. 't Ljocht wie by ús noch op. Doe hat ús heit him dat út brocht hwant hy doarst dêr net wer allinne lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ103307","role":"member","render":{"description":"A man once saw a woman in white approaching. Because he thought he knew her, he wanted to greet her, but when he came closer she went up in smoke.","place":"Drogeham","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37235","original":"In man fan Droegeham (it wie Hindrik Hoeksma sels) seach op in joun op 'e Ikkers in frommes yn 't wyt oankommen.\nHy miende dat er har wol koe en soe har groetsje. Mar doe't er flakby wie, wie se samar ynienen fuort troch in daem. Der wie neat mear fan har to sjen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA000103","role":"member","render":{"description":"Early in the morning a man sees a white woman.","place":"Hemelum","prov":"Fr.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130174","original":"Oer de Lytse Maren sjocht men op ’e eftergroun de Wite Burch. Dêr seach men eren wite wiven. In man fan Himmelom, Melchers hjitte er, gie op in moarn ier en bitiid to ikeboskjen, en seach dêr yn in iepen plak tsjin de Wite Burch oan in wyt wiif omdoarmjen.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ053715","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man once had an encounter. He was roughly thrown about by the figure.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25414","original":"Alde Rinse de Wind fan 'e Harkema hat ek us in ûntmoeting hawn. Dy waerd dêrby ek smiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Boornbergum belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.1679,"rank":1.0,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015603","role":"card","render":{"description":"A fisherman sees a lady in white clothes and decides to follow her. But the wit wief (white woman) vanishes as quickly as she appeared.","place":"Broeksterwâld","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19893","original":"Douwe syn broer Anne Feddema hie to fiskjen west. Hy hie nei 't tichtset ta west en farde de Lyts út wei werom de kant nei de brêge út. Doe kom der in juffer oan yn sniewite klean. Hy tocht: Ik wol wite hwer't dy keart, dat hy hie 't eech net fan har ôf. Doe't er oan har ta wie, died er de fêstsetter yn 'e kant en krekt doe't er dat die, wie de wite juffer fuort.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV010904","role":"card","render":{"description":"A maid living with two wicked men stabs one of the men to death and flees. The other man pursues her and, just as she shuts the stable door, throws an axe after her. The axe was fixed in the stable door of a new farmhouse as a reminder.","place":"Ter Borg","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43395","original":"Mien mouder vertelde mie n verhoal dat in Roswinkel gebeurd is. \n\nWazzen n moal twai heksn, dai n kind stooln. \nZe brochden dat kind noar twai keerls tou. \nDoor wur ze meid, man zai kreeg dr ook n stuk of wat kinder bie. \nTwintig joar is ze dr wol west.  De keerls leefden van roof en stelerij. \n Op n dag was de aine keerl vot. De ander mos eevn scheerd worn. \nt Wicht grip t mes en snit de kerel de haals oet. En dou dr vandeur. Man intied komp de ander in hoes en zug wat er gebeurd is. Hai grip de haksebiele en neit achter t wicht aan.  \nIn Roswinkel hef hai heur inhoald. Hai smit de biele op heur, man t is net te loat; zai was net n boerderij inloopn en har de voldeure achter zuk tou trokn. Door kwam de biele in terechte. …","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070b","role":"card","render":{"description":"There was once a man who went with his dog cart from Hardegarijp to Bergum. A white figure travelled with him the whole way.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12147","original":"Wite juffers\nDer wie ris in man, dy reizge mei de hûnekarre de Simmerdyk del fan Hurdegaryp nei Burgum. It wie jûn en tige mistich. Hy siet yn 'e hûnekarre en njonken him siet in wite gestalte. De hiele tiid is dy njonken him meireizge, oan Burgum ta. Dy man hat in benaud oerke trochmakke.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST075","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a wedding one of the guests remarks that they forgot to invite the witte wieven (white women). When someone mockingly calls out to the witte wieven, an axe is thrown at his head. He just manages to flee inside in time. The door still shows the marks of the axe. The witte wief (white woman) calls out that she could have caught him if she had not lost her little shoe.","place":"Zenderen","prov":"Ov.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"M.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13289","original":"Parallel met het verhaal van de \"spinvisite\" loopt ook 't verhaal van de \"brulfte\" (bruiloft) waar een van de gasten tegen de \"brulfteneugers\" opmerkt dat hij de \"nögste noabers\" n.l. de \"witte wieve\" heeft vergeten. De \"brulfteneuger\" laat dat niet op zich zitten, gaat naar buiten en nodigt \"de witte wieve\" uit, op spottende toon. Hij wordt onmiddelijk achterna gezeten, vlucht nog net binnenshuis, terwijl hem de bijl nagegooid wordt en 'n snee in de niendeure maakt die nog aan de kleinkinderen van het bruidspaar vertoond wordt. Hier hoort ook weer dezelfde klacht over 't schoentje bij, dat niet was vastgestrikt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"TINNEV065","role":"sill","render":{"description":"A man goes to cut grass stalks with six others when the first man suddenly starts screaming. The group starts running. When they have stopped running, the first man tells them he saw a grijze juffer (grey lady).","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0310F","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22411","stain":"six"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmer has two sons. One cannot be got out of bed in the morning, the other has to do all the work. At some point he is fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12173","original":"It spoek yn 'e Foksegatten\nDe wei fan Feanwâldsterwâl nei Hurdegaryp troch de Foksegatten wie foarhinne in sânreed. Op healwei stie yn in bocht in boerespul, dêr't in famylje de Vries op wenne. Twa fan 'e soannen slepten yn it bûthûsbedsteed. Ien fan 'e jonges wie moarns min fan 't bêd te krijen en dan strûpte de oare foar 't wurk op. Dêr krige dy syn nocht fan en op in moarntiid kaam er foar 't bêd mei in tuolle yn 'e hân. Hy woe him in tikje jaan om him wekker te krijen, mar hy rekke him by ûngelok oan 'e sliep, dat er it bestoar. Syn folk wie slim oerstjoer en ferslein, foaral de broer, dy't himsels ferwiet, dat er net better oppast hie.\nDe famylje koe der net langer bankje en fûn in oar hinnekommen. De pleats waard ôfbrutsen. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with D.","Didam. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"window","text":"Didam"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":6,"card":"c5","word":"six","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.679,"rank":0.375,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST274","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a wolf at night disappears when the farmer finds a wolfskin under his bed and burns it.","place":"Drogteropslagen","prov":"Dr.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"K.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13538","original":"Vroeger was hier een knecht, die 's nachts in een wolf veranderde en het de mensen dan lastig maakte. Onder zijn bed vond de boer op zekere dag een wolfshuid en verbrandde die. Sedert was de knecht verdwenen.\n(Verteld door een zeventig-jarige).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL301","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand becomes a werewolf by means of a leather belt, which he hides. It is found and burnt in the oven; at once the suspected farmhand comes rushing up on horseback, but he is held back, and when the belt has burnt he says: \"I am freed!\"","place":"Echt","prov":"L.","year":1920,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"F.S.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35840","original":"De weerwolf \n\nOp de hoeve Bosscherhof woonde eertijds een knecht die een lederen riem bezat, welke de macht had, hem, indien hij hem omgordde, te betoveren als weerwolf. Geheimzinnig en zorgvuldig werd deze band telkenmale door de knecht verstopt en wat men ook deed, hoe men ook spiedde, men vond hem nooit. En geregeld hadden de mensen uit de omtrek, die laat huiswaarts keerden, de weerwolf te dragen. En ook iedereen herkende steeds de knecht. Men gaf elkander raad om wanneer men overvallen werd, de weerwolf op een of andere manier te prikken of te krab-ben tot hij bloed voelde of zag. Dan was men gered. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Limburg an animal was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1920.","That card names an animal. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"b34e2a0079a570cd","accepted_hashes":["01315076a3d79dcf465ad73b39a9c26d8725df0f062fc37f0167891f79bfcfff","5f6ecf1dab91aa6e58945809a9e54d925ec4ab486eb1e975c6a7d666ac76efc8","b3e99f5a5bc7a8ac962fc2582311332af954f9ecbed889102a05fd95084f28fe","ee67de60cd50f29ed0369a19aa6ddcded8668b14d2252422c87a411737ced4cd","fa2f3daf86793659a4a73919bd33e18ddecceefc8acaa99faee7faddcd4136ab"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0563,"rank":0.462,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LINSSEN007605","role":"member","render":{"description":"Boy can change into a werewolf; after blood is drawn from the wolfhound, the boy's form appears.","place":"Leveroy","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208819","original":"Weerwolf. Een jongen bezat de macht om zich in een weerwolf te kunnen veranderen. Hij had verkering. Op zekere dag was hij met zijn aanstaande naar de kermis gegaan. In het struikgewas langs de weg gaf hij voor zijn behoefte te moeten doen. Tegen zijn verloofde zei hij, dat ze niet moest schrikken als er plotseling een wolf of een hond voorbij kwam. Het meisje werd bang, liep door en begaf zich naar een café, waar ze geheel onthutst aankwam. Nauwelijks was ze binnen of een wolfshond ging liggen onder de tafel, waaraan zij zat. Een van de aanwezigen had kwade vermoedens over het dier. Wanneer het een weerwolf was, zou hij nadat hem \"bloed\" getrokken was, weer een menselijke gedaante aannemen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ENGELS003711","role":"member","render":{"description":"After a fight with a werewolf it turns out to be someone known.","place":"Blerick","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210804","original":"Weerwolven:\nEen man, die ’s avonds laat door een weerwolf werd besprongen, was hem te gauw af, door zich bliksemsnel om te draaien. Hij kreeg hem er onder. Het bleek een goede bekende van hem te zijn.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"GENDT088","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"One evening a woman meets a miller's hand who has a werewolf walking behind him. The man does not see it and the wolf disappears. That spot is haunted.","place":"Gendt","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"M.H.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/49723","original":"Ik kwam soaves es ’n keer Jans, de möldersknecht van Hoogveld, tège. Achter ’m liep ’n lillek dier. ’t Leek ’n werwolf. Hé’j had grote klauwe en gloeiende oge. Ik zèj: “Wa hè gé’j dor toch bé’j ou, Jans?” Hé’j zej:“Ik heb niks bé’j mien”. En toe was er ok niks mer. Da gebeurde op ten hoek bé’j de meule. De minse zèje, dat ’t dor altied spokte.","lang":"Gendt dialect (Achterhoek)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LINSSEN008310","role":"member","render":{"description":"After the werewolf that tries to jump on someone's back is wounded, it disappears.","place":"Posterholt","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208887","original":"Weerwolf Een jongeman uit de buurtschap Holst had kennis met een meisje uit de buurtschap Paalder (st. Odilienberg). Meermalen had hij over een grote afstand de weerwolf moeten dragen. Hij had bij anderen raad gevraagd, wat hij daartegen kon doen. Men had hem aangeraden een snijmes (groot breed mes, ongeveer 6o cm lang en 1o cm breed , om stro te snijden met aan beide kanten een houten handvat.) op de rug te binden met de scherpe kant naar achteren gericht. Zo gezegd, zo gedaan. De eerstvolgende keer dat de weerwolf hem weer besprong liet deze een rauwe kreet horen, vluchtte weg en nooit meer had de man last van hem gehad.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Gendt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0476,"rank":0.4103,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ044011","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. You must never quarrel with a werewolf, because then he will kill you. A girl always did sewing at other people's homes. Her suitor once asked her for a handkerchief. She gave it to him, and outside he tore the thing to shreds. After that he was normal again. He turned out to be a werewolf. Then the girl broke it off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24049","original":"Ien fan sawn soannen wie in wjerwolf. As in wjerwolf jin kriget, makket er jin dea, seinen se froeger tsjin ús. Men mat der noait rûzje mei krije, sei in muoike yn 'e Westerein, dan pakke se jo.\nMyn wiif hat in kammeraetske hawn, dy naeide altyd by oare minsken. Dy hie forkearing mei in feint.\nOp in kear wie er by har, doe frege er har om har bûsdoek. Hja hie him de bûsdoek jown, mar doe hied er dy bûsdoek yn alle moster forskuord bûtendoar.\nLetter wie er wer goed west, mar 't is wol útrekke tusken dy beiden. Hwant hy wie in wjerwolf.\nHja hat it sels oan myn wiif forteld. Dat kammeraetske wenne oan it Wyldpaed.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST189","role":"card","render":{"description":"Three people tell that late one evening they met a big dog with fiery eyes that jumped on their backs. Only at the edge of the field did it jump off and vanish. The dog vanished near a farm already known as uncanny, because the farmhand there said that the cows several times jumped up at the stroke of midnight while the stable doors flew open by themselves.","place":"Puiflijk","prov":"Gld.","year":1957,"code":"SINSAG 0801","initials":"C.v.d.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13453","original":"Spookdieren\nMij is eens door drie verschillende personen op zeer verschillende tijden meegedeeld dat op de Waaldijk tussen Boven-Leeuwen en Druten 's avonds in pikdonker plotseling een abnormale grote hond, die plotseling verscheen, hen zwijgend met vurige ogen volgde en even plots aan de grens van Druten verdween. Beide personen waren niet bijgelovig maar hadden van angst 't zweet op de rug staan van angst, temeer daar de hond verdween bij een boerderij waar 't niet \"pluis\" scheen te zijn. Een knecht op deze boerderij vertelde mij eens hoe verscheidene malen 's nachts de koeien om klokslag 12 uur opsprongen en staldeuren openvlogen zonder 'n aanwijsbare oorzaak. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"TINNEV042","role":"door","render":{"description":"Two men are looking for grass stalks to cut. When they find none, they go home. After they have parted, one of the men suddenly sees a large wolf on his path. The next morning the other man asks him whether he saw the wolf.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22388","original":"29.\nPeter ging op een kier met Dorus mieskes sni'je. Mao zi'j konne de gin vinne en wolle daorum weer op huus aan. De weg liep deur een buske. Dorus vroeg aan Peter offe um nao huus sol brenge. \"Loop nao da galg\", antwore Peter en kroap onder de scheibeum nève de weg hèèr.\n\"Hi'j is ter\", riep Dorus um nao. Ienéns stong d'r een grote wolf op de bosweg. Hi'j wol niet op zied gaon. Daorum drèèje Peter de met een flinken boag umhen. Toe e is umkek zag e niks meer. Umdat Peter geld neudig had ginge de 's marges weer op uut um smele te zuke. Ien Kilder was Dorus al met een groten trop aan 't sni'je. Toe hi'j Peter zag riep tem toe: \"Wasse d'r now, of niet?\".","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An even number.","2 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"door","n":2},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P1","difficulty":0.7818,"rank":0.6374,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEMP259","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man who moved a boundary stone had to wander around the misplaced stone until someone released him. A drunken farmer released him by recklessly shouting that the spirit should put the stone back where he had taken it from. From then on the stone was in the right place again.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":"SINSAG 0404","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43249","original":"De reinsteen\n\nOp de Bergerstraat onder Amby werd 's nachts dikwijls een gedaante gezien, die bezig was een reinsteen te verplaatsen.\nEen knecht die laat groenten uit het veld haalde, had er zijn overleden meester in herkend. Een meisje van dezelfde boerderij had het spook ook ontmoet en herkend en was twee dagen later aan een geheimzinnige ziekte gestorven.\nOp zekere avond, het was al laat, kwam er ook een dronken boer door het veld en zag het spook weer bezig met de reinsteen. Hij hoorde het steunen en klagen: 'Waar leg ik hem! Waar leg ik hem!' Toen de boer naderbij gekomen was, kwam de geest op hem af en herhaalde ook nu zijn vraag. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST005","role":"card","render":{"description":"The soul of a dead person finds no rest if that person moved boundary stones during his life. After his death his soul must wander with the stone in his hand until he has found the right place for it. The priest advises the local farmers to tell the soul to put the stone down where he got it. A brave farmer's son does indeed say this to the soul, after which the stone falls into the right place.","place":"Arcen","prov":"L.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0404","initials":"J.J.v.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13219","original":"'t Spook\nDe ziel van een overledene welke grensstenen had verlegd, had geen rust en zweefde 's avonds door de velden roepende: \"waar zal ik hem laten.\" Op advies van de dorpspastoor moesten de boeren antwoorden: \"Waar je hem gekregen hebt.\" Een kranige boerenzoon waagde dit op een avond als tegenantwoord te geven en met een doffe plof viel de steen neer op zijn plaats.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"ENGELS000205","role":"card","render":{"description":"A boundary-stone mover who asks on his deathbed where he should leave the stone is told: where the stone came from.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0404","initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/57979","original":"Grensstenen verplaatsen:\n“Dreessen Tiesj” een boer van de van de vorige generatie, wonende aan Eyndt, nam het niet erg nauw met de eerlijkheid, en was steeds op uitbreiding van zijn aards bezit, in letterlijke zin, bedacht. Hij ploegde meestal enige voren van zijn buurman bij zijn land, en er werd beweerd, dat hij stiekem de grensstenen verlegde. Op zijn sterfbed plaagde hem zijn geweten, en lag hij te kermen en te kreunen: “Oe mot ich um toch laote?” Zijn buurman, Iezeren Henneske, die bij hem waakte, en een man, die nooit geen blad voor de mond nam, werd genoemd, wees hem terecht: “Legk um neer, oes te um gekregen hees!”\n\nOmzetting in Heldens dialect van de verhalen, ingezonden onder no. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELS001003","role":"card","render":{"description":"Hearing a voice at night asking where the boundary stone should be put down.","place":"Helden","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0404","initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210416","original":"Mensen, die grensstenen verplaatsen:\nIk heb wel eens gehoord, dat iemand, die ging kaarten ’s avonds, een stem in de lucht hoorde, die om hulp zuchtte, om een grenssteen weer op zijn juiste plaats te leggen.\n\nVerslag 57, Omzetting vanuit de Ned. taal in Heldens dialect van de verhalen, opgenomen onder no. L291-10 van verteller Frans Dorssers, Helden. Helden, 5-2-1970.\nEemes, dè s’aovens gong kaarten, huurden in ’t veldj eemes zeuchten en öm hölp vraoge. Hè zoo doonde zien geweest, öm enne paol, dè e vreuger verlaogd hei, wèr op zien gooi plats te legke.","lang":"Standard Dutch; Limburgish","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with S. 5 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"b34e2a0079a570cd","accepted_hashes":["134e55edc2675227fc47cdc8008370eaefc889624cdd0b452fbfdc12fb39502d","1a394c5c0a8c354d00c6865ca51977b12ccef98b0333f517553746efddf45e8f","d8fd565bea108e597e71053cdc0bf76958c215bc8ced0994b33dc5e4ef8f7116","ed27401eb3469db612e8b60286567e43d4310b8332a7c595b575ee9ad7eebc2b"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3656,"rank":1.0259,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053402","role":"member","render":{"description":"It sometimes happens that a dead person cannot find rest because a promise made to him was not kept. If the minister addresses the dead about his unfulfilled wish and that wish is then fulfilled, the dead finds rest. If something still has to be handed to the dead, you must roll it up in a handkerchief and hold the corner of the handkerchief. If you do not do it this way, your skin will be scorched off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25362","original":"It gebeurt soms wol us, dat ien dy't to hôf brocht is de rêst net fynt. Dan komt er wer. Meastal mat er dan hwat ha. De doomny freget him dan wol faek hwer't er forlet fan hat. Dan neamt er dat.\nAs men him dat jowt komt er net wer.\nMar men mat goed oppasse hoe't men it him jowt. Men mat it yn in bûsdoek byelkoar rolje en in tippe fan 'e bûsdoek fêsthâlde. Sa mat men it him jaen. Oars skroeit it fel der ôf. De bûsdoek skroeit nou.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CBOEK305","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Another ghost story tells of a lady in a white veil who comes through the wall between twelve and one o'clock. If anyone disturbs her rest, she wrings his neck. A strong man goes to the castle she haunts at night and destroys her for good.","place":"Driebergen-Rijsenburg","prov":"Utr.","year":1892,"code":null,"initials":"M.R.v.d.V.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/34810","original":"Een Spookgeschiedenis\nEen spookgeschiedenis zooals deze is er nog een, waarin eene geheimzinnige witgesluierde Dame het spook is; welke eveneens tusschen 12 en 1 uur komt, maar door den muur heen in de slaapkamer en roept, (wanneer zij iemand in de kamer ziet, welke het spook dooden wil), met een holle, nare grafstem: \"Wie stoort hier mijn rust?\" Daarop loopt zij toornig op den bevenden man toe en draait hem den hals om; daarna verdwijnt zij weer door den muur, alhoewel er geen deur in is. Nu durft niemand meer te wagen op het kasteel een nacht te slapen; totdat er eindelijk een moedige sterken man komt, op 't slot des nachts gaat en de witte Dame voor altijd verdelgt...\n(Breedvoerig ken ik deze historie niet meer.)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ111728","role":"member","render":{"description":"When the dead keep wandering after their death, they cannot find rest because they did something wrong or because a promise made to them was not kept. The souls of murdered people also wander at night. A man who treated his wife badly during her life is constantly harassed by her ghost after her death.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29939","original":"Soms dwaelden der minsken op 'e paden om dy't al stoarn wienen. Dy hienen hwat útheefd en koenen de rêst net fine. Of se hienen noch in bigearte, dy't earst yn forfulling gean moest.\nEk guon dy't formoarde wienen dwelmen nachts om. Yn Kollumersweach wie in wiif stoarn, dy har man hie har min bihandele. Nei har dea kaem se hyltyd wer by dy man. Soms roun se njonken him lâns. Hy koe har net wer kwyt wurde.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ002908","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman dies in Egypte and visits her husband every day. The man fetches the minister and the woman tells the minister what she desires. The man does what the woman wants and since then there has been no more haunting.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1950,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/15731","original":"Yn Egypte wenne in man, dy syn wyfke forstoar, mar nei har dea kom se alle dagen by him. Hy helle de dûmny der by, dy't har oanspruts en frege hwat se bigearde. Oan dy dûmny joech se har bigearte to witen. De man foldie oan dy bigearte en it spoekjen wie dien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Driebergen-Rijsenburg belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1867,"rank":0.6667,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ011305","role":"top","render":{"description":"Once when a man was out in the field, a very small brown dog floated past him. It headed for the canal.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17744","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ011305","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"The man asked what the dog wanted, but the little creature disappeared into the water. Exactly three weeks later the same thing happened to the man's father. Then too the dog seemed to disappear into the canal. The place was uncanny.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478","stain":"three"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"INZ00039","role":"half","render":{"description":"But the mocking voice of the mountain spirit is heard saying that the treasure can no longer be found. A girl promises to marry, and if the marriage does not happen, to give a barrel of oil for the sanctuary lamp in the church. She marries someone else anyway, forgets her promise and dies. Her restless soul returns, but a clergyman manages to banish the ghost. Her plaintive voice is still heard: they could have helped me, but they would not.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0410"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEUNING007203","role":"half","render":{"description":"When approached, the figure grows smaller and smaller, and when it is struck at, it is gone.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ060007","role":"half","render":{"description":"One day he goes to see her, and between the churchyard and the state school he sees her sitting on the right side of the path wrapped in a black cloth. He becomes frightened and returns home. Later it turns out that Griet was never there that day.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP328","role":"half","render":{"description":"The parish priest finds out and one night helps the ghost priest finish the mass. The priest thanks him: during his life he had been negligent at mass, so after his death he could find no rest, but now he is released. The priest prays so fervently for the parish priest's salvation that the latter dies after only half a year.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ060905","role":"half","render":{"description":"When Schopper, the director of the Wilhelminahoeve, hears this he does not believe it, but he has to admit she is right when they see it themselves too.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0477"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘dog’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0478. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c2","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c2"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1","word":"three","stained":"c2"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
